{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Give ear, O heavens</b> — by way of the plain sense, Ibn Ezra's words are correct, for the verses call upon the heavens and the earth as witnesses in all matters that they endure and persist, as in \"Hear, O mountains, the riv of YHWH\" (Micah 6:2), and likewise the stone of Joshua, for there it is written (Joshua 24:27) \"for it has heard.\" And by way of truth, they are the first heavens and earth mentioned in Genesis, for they entered into the covenant with Israel. Therefore he said that the heavens should give ear and the earth hear the terms, and how He will act upon them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:57:42.902196308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}